<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:44:35 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>France braces for new wave of protests, govt warns of 'very high' violence risk</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-france-braces-for-new-wave-of-protests-govt-warns-of-very-high-violence-risk</link><description>
France's interior minister on Thursday warned of a "very high risk of public disorder" and announced the deployment of around 70,000 police officers for a new wave of protests this weekend. France has been rocked by widespread anger over the rising cost of living and inequality, with nationwide demonstrations on October 17 degenerating into some of the country's worst rioting in years. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Rochelle Ferguson Bouyahi tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e871e8e8-d466-11f1-8ef8-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-140225-140855-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e871e8e8-d466-11f1-8ef8-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-140225-140855-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ee11c106-d466-11f1-889c-772010c622eb</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:35:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Black Sea shipping under growing threats as drones hit container ships</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/black-sea-shipping-under-growing-threats-as-drones-hit-container-ships</link><description>
A Greek container ship has sunk after being struck by three drones, potentially of Russian origin, in the Black Sea off the Bulgarian coast on Wednesday, October 28. This incident highlights growing concerns for commercial shipping as the conflict between Ukraine and Russia persists.
 

</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cdb01a4-b353-11f1-b596-994e92b1193e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8KZ4GJ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cdb01a4-b353-11f1-b596-994e92b1193e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8KZ4GJ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7642c680-d46a-11f1-8213-1983d418e914</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:27:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>'The Phantom of the Opera' haunts French cinemas again</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261030-the-phantom-of-the-opera-haunts-french-cinemas-again</link><description>
In this edition of arts24, "Le Fantôme de l'Opéra" returns to French cinemas in a contemporary reinterpretation starring Deva Cassel and Romain Duris. We take a closer look.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17d33b4c-d461-11f1-ad80-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-40f64497.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17d33b4c-d461-11f1-ad80-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-40f64497.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d46351e8-d461-11f1-9b6d-8dcc63788a26</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:24:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charlotte Lam</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spanish transport minister faces calls to quit after deadly train crash</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-spanish-transport-minister-faces-calls-to-quit-after-deadly-train-crash</link><description>
Spanish Transport Minister Oscar Puente faced calls to resign but ruled out stepping down on Friday. This follows Wednesday’s train crash in Toledo province, which killed 69 people. It is the country’s second high-speed rail disaster this year. FRANCE 24 correspondent Sarah Morris reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d06759c-d466-11f1-b9be-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c7b7c37f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d06759c-d466-11f1-b9be-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c7b7c37f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dd9cac8c-d45c-11f1-9e93-e113a1b2af21</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:21:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Third weekend of protests looms as tensions persist across France</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-third-weekend-of-protests-looms-as-tensions-persist-across-france</link><description>
For the third Saturday in a row, people across France are set to take to the streets to protest against the high cost of living and demand better funding for education. Police are preparing for all eventualities ahead of another weekend of protests, following earlier demonstrations that ended in rioting and looting in city centres.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e9a2506c-d45d-11f1-951a-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-130927-131111-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e9a2506c-d45d-11f1-951a-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-130927-131111-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ef086032-d45d-11f1-95c7-33050cbd318a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:10:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Who is Kevin T., the main suspect behind the racist Trappes attack?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/who-is-kevin-t-the-main-suspect-behind-the-racist-trappes-attack</link><description>
France's anti-terrorism prosecutor on Thursday released details of the main suspect in the racist attack in Trappes and La Verriere, on the outskirts of Paris, on October 23.The 39-year-old opened fire with a submachine gun, killing 26-year-old Pengo Bossio Wangi and injuring five others.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aeadaf9c-d467-11f1-8aab-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-10-30-at-14-23-41.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aeadaf9c-d467-11f1-8aab-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-10-30-at-14-23-41.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6c1211c-d467-11f1-84fe-aba2da1ce04f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:06:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The 51%</category><title>How will the women's vote shape the US midterms?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261030-how-will-the-women-s-vote-shape-the-us-midterms</link><description>
With the US midterms approaching, we examine the power of the women's vote in an election that will shape the balance of power in Washington during Donald Trump’s final two years in office. Annette Young talks to Annie Karni, congressional correspondent for The New York Times and Kelly Dittmar, Director of Research at the Centre for American Women and Politics.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e8dc1a2-d465-11f1-bafa-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/web-photo-51-percent-midterms.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e8dc1a2-d465-11f1-bafa-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/web-photo-51-percent-midterms.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ed2bea6e-d466-11f1-bc3d-417feb7fc806</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:52:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Annette YOUNG</dc:creator></item><item><category>Technology</category><title>How the record-breaking $6.3 billion heist in crypto history unfolded</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20261030-how-the-record-breaking-6-3-billion-heist-in-crypto-history-unfolded</link><description>
Hackers stole $6.3 billion in cryptocurrency from Binance in a record-breaking heist, prompting issuers to freeze roughly half of the stolen assets. The breach, which US analysts suspect was done by North Korean hackers, has shaken confidence in the crypto market.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce79d554-d452-11f1-98a4-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/Binance-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce79d554-d452-11f1-98a4-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/Binance-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d066979a-d465-11f1-b3f7-317d0b2acc30</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:52:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce79d554-d452-11f1-98a4-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/Binance-2.jpg">© Dado Ruvic, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Revisited</category><title>Georgia's European dream left in limbo</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261030-georgia-s-european-dream-left-in-limbo</link><description>
Two years ago in Georgia, tens of thousands of pro-European protesters rallied against the disputed results of the October 2024 parliamentary election, which was officially won by the ruling Georgian Dream party. A few weeks later, the authorities announced the suspension of the country's European Union accession process. Despite an ongoing crackdown, smaller-scale protests continue every day in the capital Tbilisi.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/71d4e250-d3ba-11f1-ad40-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/billet-retour-EN-1.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/71d4e250-d3ba-11f1-ad40-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/billet-retour-EN-1.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cb199ede-d2eb-11f1-b617-d17d6f2c4016</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:34:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Maria GERTH-NICULESCU</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Texas Republicans accused of changing electoral rules ahead of midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261030-texas-republicans-accused-of-changing-electoral-rules-ahead-of-midterms</link><description>
With the US midterm elections approaching, Republicans in Texas are being accused of changing electoral rules in their favour. In Tarrant County, near Dallas, they've cut the number of election-day polling places by nearly 30 percent. The decision is being challenged in court and adds to last year's state-wide redistricting, a move designed to benefit Republicans. But the measures could also help galvanise the Democratic opposition. FRANCE 24's Pierrick Leurent reports, with Wassim Cornet.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cba8206-d3be-11f1-a12f-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-USA-TEXAS-GERRYMANDERING-BAIN-Lauren.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cba8206-d3be-11f1-a12f-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-USA-TEXAS-GERRYMANDERING-BAIN-Lauren.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7d5933fc-d3be-11f1-85c4-6facf1c0b072</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:07:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Pierrick LEURENT</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Ukraine war live: Russian strikes leave 200,000 without power in Ukraine's Dnipropetrovsk region</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-live-russia-strikes-energy-facilities-kyiv-aid-convoy-heads-besieged-town-oleshky-ukraine</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">bf4971f2-d461-11f1-a9e9-abdb486587bc</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:59:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>‘Scared of crossing the border’: The Arizona farmers who rely on Mexican workers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261030-scared-of-crossing-the-border-the-arizona-farmers-who-rely-on-mexican-workers</link><description>
The vast produce farms of Yuma County, Arizona, rely heavily on foreign workers who cross the border every day from Mexico. John Boelts, a farmer and staunch supporter of US President Donald Trump, praises the administration’s strict border controls – though he says that competing Republican factions have complicated efforts to hire foreign labourers.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e2330d6-cbd4-11f1-a9eb-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/main-dans-les-champs.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e2330d6-cbd4-11f1-a9eb-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/main-dans-les-champs.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f106d570-d44f-11f1-a61e-a30f742156bf</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:28:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e2330d6-cbd4-11f1-a9eb-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/main-dans-les-champs.jpg">© Barbara Gabel, FRANCE 24</source><dc:creator>Barbara GABEL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia recruits Africans to fight in Ukraine, families seek answers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russia-recruits-africans-to-fight-in-ukraine-families-seek-answers</link><description>
While African leaders and Russian officials gather to discuss security, trade and political cooperation at the Africa-Russia summit, one sensitive issue is notably absent from the agenda: the recruitment of Africans to fight for Russia in Ukraine. More than 1,400 Africans have been enlisted since 2023. In Tunisia, concern is growing as the families of several men who travelled to Russia for work or study are still searching for answers about the fate of their loved ones. FRANCE 24's team in Tunisia reports. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3f32cba-d44b-11f1-873d-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-dc16521b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3f32cba-d44b-11f1-873d-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-dc16521b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d93e6f8a-d444-11f1-aaf8-15429d64cfb0</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:06:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Access Asia</category><title>Foiled Hindu temple plot exposes rising anti-Indian sentiment in the US</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261030-foiled-hindu-temple-plot-exposes-rising-anti-indian-sentiment-in-the-us</link><description>
In this edition of Access Asia, we explore why anti-Indian sentiment is rising in the United States in the wake of the foiled plot targeting a Hindu temple in Illinois. We ask the executive director of the Center for the Study of Organized Hate what's behind the trend, and whether the rhetoric coming from the Trump White House is to blame.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c141a4ba-d3b3-11f1-ba9c-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-PHOTO-ind%C3%A9pendance-indienne.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c141a4ba-d3b3-11f1-ba9c-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-PHOTO-ind%C3%A9pendance-indienne.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c50d131c-d38c-11f1-ad2e-6b9c3c15f12d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:02:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Delano D’SOUZA</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>At least 60 Christians killed in Ethiopia amid rising religious violence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-at-least-60-christians-killed-in-ethiopia-amid-rising-religious-violence</link><description>
At least 60 Christians have been killed in Ethiopia in what the Orthodox Church has declared as religious violence. It is still unclear who was behind the attack, with rebels and local government blaming each other. Around 20 houses have been burned down, as FRANCE 24's correspondent Tom Canetti reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b965392-d44c-11f1-9c71-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-46bebd36.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b965392-d44c-11f1-9c71-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-46bebd36.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d327128a-d446-11f1-94a8-c5ddd4874f79</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:01:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Senegal gears up for historic 2026 Youth Olympic Games in Dakar</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-senegal-gears-up-for-historic-2026-youth-olympic-games-in-dakar</link><description>
The International Olympic Committee is upbeat just 24 hours before competition gets under way at the 2026 Youth Olympic Games in Senegal. Venues are ready to host the first-ever Olympic event on the African continent. FRANCE 24's correspondent Aminatou Diallo reports from the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b53b7c32-d44d-11f1-ada0-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6cca01f2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b53b7c32-d44d-11f1-ada0-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6cca01f2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">31bfe5a2-d44b-11f1-aad5-6df4798b8782</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:58:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Tanzania: 2025 election violence still traumatises, one year on</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-tanzania-2025-election-violence-still-traumatises-one-year-on</link><description>
Tanzania is marking the first anniversary of a bloody election that left many traumatised. The October 29, 2025 election, in which President Samia Suluhu Hassan won with 98 percent of the vote after most of the opposition was excluded, triggered days of protests that security forces brutally suppressed. Many government critics say they still fear abduction, arbitrary arrest and politically motivated prosecutions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6cfc6408-d44e-11f1-b7a8-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5fb1d914.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6cfc6408-d44e-11f1-b7a8-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5fb1d914.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bb5f5748-d44b-11f1-822e-7fb8cd2f846a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:55:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>TotalEnergies posts record profits as it keeps a lid on fuel prices</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-totalenergies-posts-record-profits-as-it-keeps-a-lid-on-fuel-prices</link><description>
As hundreds of thousands across France are expected to take to the street again this weekend to protest the high cost of living, oil and gas giant TotalEnergies has posted record profits for the quarter to September. The company has kept fuel prices lower than rivals at its pumps, but motorists are wondering whether it could bring them lower still.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17e3b08a-d44d-11f1-b8d0-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-110830-111004-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17e3b08a-d44d-11f1-b8d0-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-110830-111004-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1cf179ae-d44d-11f1-98a4-8d24f1bca529</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:40:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Tennis: Alexander Zverev guaranteed to become world No. 1</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261030-tennis-alexander-zverev-guaranteed-to-become-world-no-1</link><description>
Alexander Zverev secured his place as the next world No. 1 by beating Tallon Griekspoor (6-4, 7-5) at the ATP 500 tournament in Vienna. The 29-year-old German will top the ATP rankings on Monday, November 2, replacing Jannik Sinner. He will become the first German world No. 1 since Boris Becker in 1991, and the 30th player in history to reach the top spot.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88beea18-d411-11f1-89a8-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/zverev.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88beea18-d411-11f1-89a8-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/zverev.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">521ec3f4-d414-11f1-b502-49d8d3203d99</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:34:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel elections: Netanyahu attacks Arab parties as they emerge as potential kingmakers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-israel-elections-netanyahu-attacks-arab-parties-as-they-emerge-as-potential-kingmakers</link><description>
Benjamin Netanyahu's Likud party alleged on Thursday, without ​providing evidence, that Arab parties' record gains in an election this week were driven in part by voter fraud. These accusations represent an escalation of anti-Arab rhetoric by Netanyahu and his far-right partners after Arab-led parties made a historic showing in the election – giving them a potential kingmaker role in the next government
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/432b1016-d449-11f1-a7f3-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-090521-090702-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/432b1016-d449-11f1-a7f3-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-090521-090702-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">48692c0c-d449-11f1-a36f-4593276b340c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:10:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel elections: Difficult negotiations lie ahead after Netanyahu's bloc lost majority</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-israel-elections-difficult-negotiations-lie-ahead-after-netanyahu-s-bloc-lost-majority</link><description>
Israel's final election results confirmed Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s bloc lost its majority of parliamentary seats and that weeks of difficult negotiations among very different parties, from ultra-Orthodox Jewish to secular to Arab-led, lie ahead. The results released early Friday showed Netanyahu’s bloc won 53 seats in Tuesday's elections. The main opposition bloc won 48. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/72be2ccc-d445-11f1-8c77-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-100113-100704-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/72be2ccc-d445-11f1-8c77-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-100113-100704-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">786a5b96-d445-11f1-8387-55f1d17ce03c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:08:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spain demands answers as train disaster toll rises</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-spain-demands-answers-as-train-disaster-toll-rises</link><description>
